---
import { ADDONS } from "../data";
import Section from "./Section.astro";
---

<Section id="addons" title="The addons it works with">
  <p>
    Ravenpost finds Classic Era, World of Warcraft: Forever and Forever's beta by itself, and shows which of these
    addons are installed in each game.
  </p>
  <ul class="mb-3.5">
    {
      ADDONS.map(({ name, url, what }) => (
        <li class="border-edge/60 m-0 flex flex-wrap gap-x-2.5 border-b py-2.5">
          <a href={url} class="min-w-42 font-semibold">
            {name}
          </a>
          <span class="text-dim">{what}</span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>
  <p class="text-dim text-[0.95rem]">
    Ravenpost sends something only for Hearthtale, WoWLocker, and, if you share what you see, Lorekeeper's Codex,
    Yonder and Second Wind. For the others, it just shows they're installed.
  </p>
</Section>
